Z||000000||rodmcneill||12-07-2001||01:19 PM||||Since its that time of year when people buy electric shavers as gifts, what are some of the good ones out there. I am still using a blade myself, I will have to try some of the triple blade shavers. Anyone out there still using a straight blade and leather strap.||||reg||6
Z||000001||btoth||12-07-2001||04:59 PM||||I tried a few different electrics... now I just use a Mach 3 because it doesn't <I>pull</I> my hair out and give my entire neck razor burn.  I have to get one of those heaters for the shaving cream for Christmas!  That'll feel good in the morning.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-07-2001||05:26 PM||||i've been using a schick twin blade disposeable that has a little dealie that pushes the hair out from bettween the two blades so it shaves better longer. but now that i have to stay clean shaven for a while i'm kind of wondering about an electric too. it's been a couple of weeks and the razor bumps (pseudofoliculitis barbi. say that 3 times real fast) are starting.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||12-07-2001||06:04 PM||||Are you shaving your face?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||12-07-2001||06:09 PM||||Mach 3 is great, I got a couple sample ones in the mail.  But I refuse to pay the prices for those blade refills.  The refills for my old Sensor are finally being sold under private label packaging, so I'm staying with that for a few more years.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||12-07-2001||06:11 PM||||I thought I would like an electric...until I tried it.  They say you won't develop a close cut for about a month, but I gave up after six months of waiting.  I didn't have a high end electric razor, but it was the triple head.  I was very very disappointed, doesn't give any sort of close shave whatsoever.<P>Now I use the Mach 3; somewhat pricy, but they shave so smooth and close it's worth it.  They're also well designed in that the triple blades clean out really easy.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||12-08-2001||01:43 AM||||Long story (ok, not too long, tried it in a pinch at a gal friend's house) but I now use a 'women's' razor.  3-blade Venus thing I belive.<P>It works very well, dosen't pull the hair out, and dosen't leave my skin all razorburnt.<P>PS: shave in the shower, with *lots* of mild soap, eg neutrogena.<P>Also, even though I need to everyday, I shave only every *other* day, which helps reset the folicles to grow more slowly (less constant stimulation, that's not dirty...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Philphine||12-08-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Are you shaving your face?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>no...just this wierd hair on the palms of my hands  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <P>yes my face. i'm full time military now. i used to just shave for drill weekends and when i had to look presentable (or as close as i could get to it). now even if my face gets irritated i have to keep shaving till it gets bad enough that maybe i can get a waiver. i'll take any tips i can get.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||12-08-2001||12:45 PM||||Seems like most of the womens' (blade, not electric) razors I've seen have these microfine wires that run perpendicular to the edges of the blades - to prevent cuts while shaving. <P>Might give those a try if other types of razors are causing you grief and excesssive irritation...<P>I second the Mach3 opinions... *awesome* razors, but I refuse to pay a buck a blade refill for those things. I use the grocery store 10-for-two-bucks twin-blade disposables now and just clean between the blades with a toothpick to get more life out of 'em.<P>If the Mach3 refills cut their price in half, they'll have me as a customer for life.||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||12-08-2001||01:44 PM||||Tried many different kinds. Always go back to my old Gillette double edge 'safety' razor. Wish I had the courage to use a straight razor, but not that adventurous. The new fangled ones just clog up too often. I will tell you something I learned in corrosion control school in the military.<BR>If you will get a little glass or coffee cup, fill it half full of baby oil, and put your razor in it each time after use, the blades last much longer, even Stainless Steel. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||12-08-2001||03:02 PM||||Wow, good advice! I'll give it a try...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||12-08-2001||10:46 PM||||I've tried rotary and screen type electrics, and ended up having to shave twice a day.  Now, I use a plain old Trac II (don't get the generic replacement blades at Wally World), and women's gel shaving cream.  Works great, and my face smells like my wife's legs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroKyle||12-09-2001||12:56 AM||||Amen to the mach 3.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">      <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||10
Z||000013||Mark Matthews||12-09-2001||01:12 AM||||Blade and mild facial soap in the shower as well.  I do have the Norelco something or other.  The one that spits the goo out, that helps a bit.  Shaving with shaving cream bothers me more than with the electric.  And damn is it quick!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(edit) - electric shave doesn't last as long tho, it's an every morning thing, for smooth anyway.  <BR>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mark Matthews (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||12-09-2001||01:15 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  I wonder if Mach10 will get depressed reading how everybody seemingly likes Mach3.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyways, I use Atra II razors with the white strip and Edge Gel: Super Sensative.  But I only shave on Monday mornings, in the shower and the rest of the week I just let it grow until the next again Monday or we have to go some place and I have to look presentable.<P>Delicate skin...but when I do shave, wife says my face is as smooth as a baby's bottom and she likes nuzzling up to me after I do.  On the other hand, she also likes the fresh unshaven look.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've had about 20 different electric shavers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon13.gif">  and have never been impressed by any of them.  After about a month, in the trash can they go.  Batteries die, won't hold the charge, nicks your face, you name it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
